WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.500
Narrator: Every match day has a run sheet.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Narrator: It counts down to kick-off.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.300
Narrator: You check in about four and a half hours before kick-off, sign in, collect your kit and eat.

4
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.550
Narrator: At three hours there is a general briefing.

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:26.600
Narrator: You deploy to your area, your supervisor briefs you in position, and two hours before kick-off you are on post.

6
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.100
Narrator: Gates open ninety minutes before kick-off.

7
00:00:31.108 --> 00:00:40.175
Narrator: During the second half you await instructions from your supervisor to move to your egress position, and after the final whistle we run egress for about two hours.

8
00:00:40.525 --> 00:00:53.125
Narrator: Then - and only then - once your supervisor gives you the stand down signal you come off post, go to the debrief, return your equipment and check out.

9
00:00:53.625 --> 00:01:01.025
Narrator: Watch for the three pressure peaks: the last half hour before kick-off, half-time, and the final whistle.

